      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "1. Check if the SmartHub is properly plugged into a power source.\n   - Verify that the power cable is securely connected to both the SmartHub and the power outlet.\n   - Ensure the power outlet is functioning by plugging in another device to confirm it provides power.\n2. Restart the SmartHub by unplugging it for 10 seconds and plugging it back in.\n   - Unplug the SmartHub from the power source.\n   - Wait for 10 seconds to allow any residual power to dissipate.\n   - Reconnect the SmartHub to the power source.\n3. Ensure the SmartHub is connected to the correct Wi-Fi network.\n   - Navigate to the SmartHub's settings menu to check the current Wi-Fi network it is connected to.\n   - Compare it with the network details on your smartphone or computer.\n   - If they do not match, disconnect the SmartHub from the current Wi-Fi network and reconnect it to the correct one.\n4. Reset the SmartHub to factory settings.\n   - Locate the reset button on the SmartHub.\n   - Press and hold the reset button for 10 seconds.\n   - Wait for the SmartHub to reboot.\n   - Note: This will erase all custom settings and configurations.\n5.",
